+# UX-NAV-03-047: Queue, search, and draft recovery - Permissions, audit, and receipts
+
+Stage evidence for the operator loop slice (`Queue, search, and draft recovery complete the operator loop`).
+
+## Base SHA and scope
+
+- Base branch: `main`, base SHA `0d2631f760f268ba9aad05b3f1b470ed14f735c1` (synced with `origin/main` before editing).
+- Changed files and why:
+
+| File | Change needed |
+| --- | --- |
+| `src/modules/queues/contracts/queue-audit.ts` (new) | Defines the persisted audit/receipt contract (`QueueAuditEventSchema`, `QueueAuditReceiptSchema` with `real`/`empty`/`blocked` states and the declared event types). |
+| `src/modules/queues/contracts/index.ts` | Exports the new audit contract. |
+| `src/modules/queues/audit-labels.ts` (new) | Commercial/product label mapping for audit event types (no implementation jargon, no secret references). |
+| `src/modules/queues/actions.ts` | Adds `requireCurrentUser()` authorization to every queue server action, scopes every mutation and draft recovery to the selected workspace's queues, and persists immutable audit events (`queue_item.created`, `queue_item.updated`, `queue_item.recovered`, `queue_item.deleted`, `sla_policy.upserted`) with safe payloads; revalidates `/search` on recovery/discard. |
+| `src/modules/queues/queries.ts` | New `getQueueItemReceipts()`: workspace-scoped read of persisted audit events joined to `users` for actor name; removes the raw `payload` column from the draft read path that feeds the UI. |
+| `src/modules/queues/queue-activity-receipt.tsx` (new) | Server component rendering the "Comprovante de atividade" receipt with distinct empty/real states and the selected workspace name. |
+| `src/app/search/page.tsx` | Auth-gates the route (`admin`, `operador`, `builder`), shows the selected workspace name on the draft recovery section, and renders the activity receipt. |
+| `src/app/admin/queues/page.tsx` | Auth-gates the manager route (`builder`, `admin`) and renders the activity receipt. |
+| `tests/unit/queue-audit-contract.test.ts` (new) | Contract tests: real/empty/blocked receipts, rejection of unknown states and invalid event shapes, commercial labels for every declared event type, no secret keywords in labels. |
+| `docs/EVIDENCE.md` | This evidence record. |
+
+## Route / screen / button affected
+
+- `/search` (Busca Global): the "Rascunhos Recuperáveis" section and the new "Comprovante de atividade" panel below it. The "Recuperar" button submits `recoverQueueItem`.
+- `/admin/queues` (Filas/SLA): the queue item management cards (Recuperar/Descartar) and the same "Comprovante de atividade" panel in the aside.
+
+## Persistence / domain / contract path
+
+- **Persistence object:** `queue_items` (draft recovery mutation `status: draft -> open`) and the immutable `events` table (workflow schema) holding the audit trail.
+- **Domain object:** queue audit event/type DTOs in `src/modules/queues/contracts/queue-audit.ts`.
+- **Use case / API path:** server actions in `src/modules/queues/actions.ts` (permission-gated, event-emitting) and the read query `getQueueItemReceipts()` in `src/modules/queues/queries.ts`.
+- **Validation evidence:** every action resolves the selected workspace via `ensureActiveWorkspaceConfig()` and requires an authenticated user via `requireCurrentUser()` before any mutation or audit write. Queue item mutations and draft recovery additionally verify the item's queue belongs to the selected workspace, so a cross-workspace id cannot be mutated or recovered.
+
+## User journey
+
+- **Operator (workspace-scoped, no Builder privilege):** enters `/search`, types a query, reviews results, reaches "Rascunhos Recuperáveis", clicks "Recuperar". The item leaves the draft list, an immutable `queue_item.recovered` event is persisted, and the receipt panel shows "Rascunho recuperado" with actor, timestamp and workspace. Return path: "Voltar ao painel" -> `/`.
+- **Blocked state:** unauthenticated visitors are redirected to `/auth/login`; profiles without access are redirected to `/blocked?role=...`; this is a distinct user-facing outcome.
+- **Empty vs real:** the receipt panel and the draft list render distinct empty messaging when no persisted rows exist; real rows render with their persisted data. No demo/synthetic fallback exists on this read path.
+- **Builder-originated:** the Builder starts at `/builder`, selects the organization and workspace (WorkspaceContext preserved), reaches the manager destination `/admin/queues`, operates queue items and draft recovery, and returns to `/admin` via the navigation card. Builder retains full profile access.
+
+## Commands executed (honest results)
+
+- `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, `git status --short`: confirmed the forced checkout.
+- `npm run check:no-explicit-any`: attempted; not runnable in the worker checkout because `node_modules` is absent (dependency bootstrap is owned by the supervisor). No explicit `any` was introduced in any new or changed file by manual review.
+- `npm run build`: delegated to the supervisor for the same reason.
+
+## Blocker
+
+None. This stage required no schema migration: the immutable `events` table already exists and is used by adjacent modules; no new columns were needed.
